    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/95718": {
      "title": "Slate and Student Success Data Administrator",
      "description": "Slate and Student Success Data Administrator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Slate and Student Success Data Administrator Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Salary Range $80,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Education Level 4 Year Degree Category Staff Apply Description About the Opportunity The Slate & Student Success Data Administrator serves as the primary system administrator and functional expert for the College’s Slate Student Success CRM instance, while also leading data projects that support student retention and success initiatives. This position is responsible for the configuration, maintenance, and ongoing optimization of Slate to support the needs of Student Success & Engagement and other College partners. This position will work with College partners to develop predictive retention models to support the needs of the Crest-to-Career project, and works closely with colleagues in Enrollment Management and Academic Affairs on Slate projects to align system capabilities and data initiatives with institutional goals and to ensure data-driven decision making that improves student outcomes. The Crest to Career project is a 5-year project support by a federal Title III Strengthening Institutions Program grant. By supporting further Slate implementation and the development of data analysis tools, this position strengthens the College’s enrollment and fiscal stability through improved data access, information sharing, and data decision-making. Key Responsibilities Slate system administration (75%) Serve as the primary Slate Captain for the Slate Student Success instance, maintaining overall system configuration and ensuring platform health. Build and maintain forms, populations, queries, rules, dashboards, reports, and portals within Slate. Design and implement automated workflows, such as those to support advising outreach, case management, and student communications. Apply process improvement techniques to identify manual workflows that can be replaced with sustainable, system-driven solutions. Partner with Student Success, Academic Advising, Financial Aid, Residential Life, and other campus units to translate operational needs into scalable Slate configurations and data solutions. Design and deliver training programs for Slate users across student success units, including onboarding sessions, user guides, and workshops. Act as the primary point of contact for day-to-day Slate support requests from functional users, investigating issues and implementing resolutions. Manage user access, roles, and permissions in compliance with institutional data governance and FERPA requirements. Oversee lifecycle planning for platform upgrades, new modules, and long-term system evolution. Monitor system performance and troubleshoot technical and functional issues, implementing solutions or escalating as appropriate. Document all system configurations, processes, and procedural changes in an administrative manual. Stay current on Slate releases, new features, and community best practices, assessing their relevance and value to the institution. Coordinate with IT colleagues to maintain and troubleshoot integrations between Slate and Jenzabar and other enterprise systems. Participate in committees and related working groups as assigned to ensure consistent data standards and stewardship across systems. Build and maintain operational reports and dashboards that provide actionable insights to student success leadership and front-line staff. Champion data quality across the Slate Student Success instance, establishing and enforcing data entry standards and validation rules. Predictive Analytics & Data Projects (25%) Partner with Information Technology, the Registrar’s Office, and Institutional Research to develop, test, and refine predictive models for student retention using data from Jenzabar and the Slate Student Success instance. Coordinate the extraction, integration, and validation of data feeds between Jenzabar and Slate to support predictive modeling. Translate model outputs (e.g., risk scores, retention indicators) into actionable Slate workflows, populations, and communication triggers for advisors and student success staff. Collaborate with stakeholders to identify new data sources and variables that could improve the accuracy and usefulness of predictive models. Monitor and report on the performance and impact of predictive models, recommending refinements based on outcomes data. Serve as a liaison between Student Success, IT, and Institutional Research on data projects related to retention, persistence, and graduation analytics. Qualifications What We're Looking For Qualifications Education Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Management Information Systems, Statistics, Higher Education, or a related field. Equivalent combination of education and experience will be considered. Experience Minimum of 3–4 years of hands-on experience building or administering Technolutions Slate or a comparable CRM platform, including building queries, forms, workflows, and portals. Experience working in or closely with a higher education student success, academic advising, or student affairs environment. Demonstrated experience with requirements gathering, business process analysis, and translating stakeholder needs into system solutions. Experience with data analysis, reporting tools, and relational database concepts, including working with ERP data (Jenzabar experience preferred). Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong understanding of Slate CRM administrative functions, including populations, rules, forms, queries, reports, and communication workflows. Familiarity with ERP integration processes (data imports/exports, sync troubleshooting), ideally with Jenzabar. Working knowledge of statistical or predictive modeling concepts as applied to student retention (e.g., regression, risk scoring), or strong aptitude and willingness to develop this skill set. Knowledge of FERPA and applicable data security and privacy standards for student information. Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously in a deadline-oriented environment with strong attention to detail. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build collaborative relationships across technical and non-technical audiences. Self-motivated and proactive in identifying opportunities to improve system performance and user experience. Commitment to equity, inclusion, and serving students from diverse backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience specifically with Slate for Student Success (as distinct from Slate for Admissions). Direct experience with Jenzabar as a data source for reporting or analytics. Hands-on experience building or supporting predictive retention models or similar institutional analytics projects. Familiarity with statistical software or languages for data analysis and modeling. Familiarity with HTML, CSS, Liquid Markup, JavaScript, or SQL for advanced Slate customization. Experience with Business Intelligence platforms such as Cognos, Power BI, or Tableau. What We Offer Be Part of a Purpose-Driven Community: Your work will help create a safe, beautiful, and inviting campus that supports learning, leadership, and civic engagement. Work in a Unique Setting: Our campus is a certified arboretum, offering the opportunity to care for a diverse collection of trees and green spaces in a historic and inspiring environment. Comprehensive Benefits: In addition to health, dental, vision, and retirement benefits, we offer a unique tuition benefit for employees and their families. While Cedar Crest is a women’s college, men can access certain classes on campus and others at partner institutions, making this benefit flexible and valuable for all. Support for Growth: We encourage professional development and provide training opportunities for team members. Campus Culture: Cedar Crest is a place where your story is valued. We see you, and we’re here to help you shape your future. How to Apply For full consideration , please submit: Current resume Cover letter highlighting your relevant experience Contact information for three professional references Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. “0” on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/87597": {
      "title": "Senior Accountant",
      "description": "Senior Accountant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Senior Accountant Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Salary Range $70,000.00 - $75,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Education Level 4 Year Degree Category Staff Apply Description About the Opportunity The Senior Accountant maintains the College’s general ledger and accounting records and is responsible for ensuring the accuracy, validity, and completeness of all financial transactions.  Prepares reconciliations of the general ledger account balances to the supporting subsidiary ledgers and other source records. Assists with the month and year-end close processes and with the preparation of schedules necessary for the year-end audit. The Senior Accountant also processes all requests for payment and generates disbursements on a weekly schedule, researches and resolves A/P problems on a timely basis and posts all procurement card expense reports. Key Responsibilities Prepare necessary journal entries for the month and year-end close process. Verify the accuracy, validity and completeness of the entries received from other departments to the general ledger.  Identify problems and potential solutions to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting. Prepare and run customized reports for the College Community as needed to facilitate budgeting and planning. Reconcile the bank statements, outstanding checks and general ledger accounts on a monthly basis.  Make corresponding journal entries to record activity or to correct any discrepancies found. Perform general ledger recalculations and maintenance within the accounting software, which includes account and business officer set up. Assist with preparation of annual tax exempt returns, Form 990 and Form 990-T. Process invoices for payment through check, ACH, Wire, or Credit Card. Assist with inquires related to payables, vendor disputes, etc. Accurately complete all College 1099’s on an annual basis. Reconcile and review Procurement card purchases and expense reports. Alert leadership to any questionable payment requests or documentation from various departments. Ensure that invoices at year-end are put in proper fiscal year and provide copies of invoices for necessary accruals. Complete and distribute invoices for applicable funds, mainly restricted grant accounts. Maintain, review, and reconcile all endowed funds on a monthly basis. Maintain the fixed asset software and spreadsheets, which includes the capitalization and depreciation of assets. Assist the Controller with the month and year-end close of the general ledger, which includes the preparation of director’s report packages and summary level reports for management and reviewing departmental balances for overages or discrepancies. Process month end reports from software for month end reconciliations. Monitor prepaid expenses/accruals on a monthly basis for necessary adjustments and update spreadsheets which track these expenses. Prepare various schedules and financial reports as required to support the College’s independent auditors. Assist in the completion of the annual financial statement, A-133, IAG and other audits. Develop and maintain other analytical spreadsheets as required. Assist in the coordination of annual budget requests, upload of the final budgets to the accounting software and generate summary reports for review and analysis. Completion of Finance Office surveys and Key Operating Data Annual Report. Ensure the College’s accounting policies and practices are in accordance with GAAP. Prepare and scan all appropriate documentation in applicable imaging software. Maintain file copies of all supporting financial records and issued reports. Maintain file copies of grants, other external funding agreements, and contracts to which the College is a party. Other duties as assigned by leadership. Qualifications What We're Looking For Education and Training Bachelor's degree in accounting (or equivalent experience) required with knowledge of GAAP. Not-for-Profit/Higher Education experience preferred. Advanced spreadsheet skills on Microsoft Excel, Access and Powersoft InfoMaker. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Working knowledge of not-for-profit accounting standards and financial issues pertinent to higher education institutions. Excellent organizational and time management skills, including the ability to successfully manage multiple tasks simultaneously and prioritize effectively to meet deadlines. Strong attention to detail with a commitment to accuracy and efficiency. Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, both verbal and written. Able to react and adapt to changing situations appropriately. Strong commitment to and focus on customer service. Commitment to confidentiality and integrity of systems and processes. Physical Requirements and Working Conditions Able to communicate both verbally and in writing with or without the use of auxiliary devices. Able to sit up to 90% of the working day and have sufficient dexterity to operate personal computer, printer, and other office equipment. Able and available to work outside of normal business hours to meet College obligations. What We Offer Be Part of a Purpose-Driven Community: Your work will help create a safe, beautiful, and inviting campus that supports learning, leadership, and civic engagement. Work in a Unique Setting: Our campus is a certified arboretum, offering the opportunity to care for a diverse collection of trees and green spaces in a historic and inspiring environment. Comprehensive Benefits: In addition to health, dental, vision, and retirement benefits, we offer a unique tuition benefit for employees and their families. While Cedar Crest is a women’s college, men can access certain classes on campus and others at partner institutions, making this benefit flexible and valuable for all. Support for Growth: We encourage professional development and provide training opportunities for team members. Campus Culture: Cedar Crest is a place where your story is valued. We see you, and we’re here to help you shape your future. How to Apply Pease submit: Current resume Cover letter highlighting your relevant experience Contact information for three professional references Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. “0” on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
