    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/57614": {
      "title": "Lifeguard",
      "description": "Lifeguard You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Lifeguard Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Salary Range $13.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Part Time Category Staff Apply Description Rodale Aquatic Center (RAC), located on the campus of Cedar Crest College, is seeking qualified Lifeguards to join our busy center on a part time basis.  RAC is dedicated to fostering civic health and wellness by providing educational opportunities to the campus and the larger community, alone and in cooperation with other organizations that enhance the development of the mind, body and spirit through a large offering of instruction and fitness classes. These part-time positions are flexible, between 10 – 25 hours per week. Qualifications Part-time afternoon and evening hours with the flexibility to extend hours throughout the day, evening and weekends.  Current lifeguarding certification required. Application Instructions Please submit a letter of interest (cover letter), resume, three references. Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. “0” on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
