    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/80301": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Nursing",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Nursing You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Nursing Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level Graduate Degree Category Adjunct Apply Position Description The School of Nursing at Cedar Crest College is seeking adjunct faculty with experience in medical-surgical nursing to join our dynamic team focused on educating future nurse leaders with quality instruction in state of the art facilities with Simulation Center.  Adjunct faculty will serve as clinical instructors for the fall 2021 semester, primarily on weekends. Qualifications Candidates for adjunct faculty must have an MSN (or be currently enrolled in and pursuing an MSN). Experience in the medical-surgical nursing required. Experience teaching in a college environment strongly preferred. Application Instructions Please submit a letter of interest (cover letter), CV, a statement of teaching philosophy, and three letters of reference. Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. “0” on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
