    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/82055": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Math",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Math You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Math Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level Graduate Degree Category Adjunct Apply Description The Department of Mathematics at Cedar Crest College invites applications for adjunct faculty to teach courses in the areas of Probability and Statistics, Precalculus, and College Mathematics.  Candidates must be available to teach courses between the hours of 8am and noon. Qualifications Qualified candidates must possess a Master’s degree or Ph.D. in mathematics or a related field. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level is required. Application Instructions A complete application includes a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three letters of reference.  At least one of the letters of reference must address teaching excellence.   Please indicate preferred courses of instruction when submitting materials.  Responses will be sent only to those under consideration. Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. “0” on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
