    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/62D4FBF25A09F3EBE58345A7B7B899F9/jobs/80467": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Art Therapy",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Art Therapy You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Art Therapy Allentown, PA 18104 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Education Level Graduate Degree Category Adjunct Apply Description Cedar Crest College seeks adjunct faculty members to teach primarily in the undergraduate art therapy program. Successful candidates may be considered for adjunct faculty openings in the graduate program as well. About the Art Therapy Major: The Art Therapy Major at the undergraduate level introduces the student to theories in art therapy and develops the student’s technical skills in multiple studio mediums. The Art Therapy undergraduate major prepares students to pursue graduate studies in Art Therapy. Qualifications Applicants from Pennsylvania and New Jersey are welcome to apply.  Adjunct faculty are required to hold a Master’s Degree in Art Therapy, be credentialed as an ATR-BC, and to have a minimum of three years professional experience. Prior experience teaching at the college level is strongly preferred. Courses are taught on campus Application Instructions Please submit a letter of interest (cover letter), CV, a statement of teaching philosophy, and three letters of reference. Jeanne Clery Act & Campus Safety Disclosure In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) and federal law, Cedar Crest College is committed to providing a safe learning environment. Our Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR) includes statistics for the previous three calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the College, and on public property within or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. The report also contains institutional policies concerning campus security, institutional disciplinary procedures, emergency notifications, and other personal safety matters. View the Digital Report: You can read or download the complete 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (PDF) on the Campus Police website: https://www.cedarcrest.edu/annualsecurityreport Request a Printed Copy: Copies of the report may also be obtained at Campus Police located in the Safety & Facilities Building or by calling 610-437-4471 (Option: 0) off campus or ext. “0” on campus. Share job details to About CEDAR CREST COLLEGE About the College Join our Team! Trailblazers. Ceiling smashers. Healers. Helpers. Artists. Advocates. Athletes. Allies. We are a community of students, faculty, staff, families, and friends who are committed to making a positive difference in our own lives and in the world around us. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
